WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:01.934
-You look fantastic.

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:03.501
Happy belated birthday,
by the way.

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:05.534
-Thank you, Jimmy.
-Yeah.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.701
You brought something that --
that related to your birthday,

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.834
because your kids made you
something very special,

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:13.200
that's something you enjoy,
that I'd never heard of.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.434
What -- What is it --
What is it called again?

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:18.300
-A chip butty.
-Yeah, a "chip butty."

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.901
Any guesses?
-Whoo!

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:22.534
-Has anyone ever heard of that?

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:24.200
Yes!
-Yeah, you're just saying that

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.834
to talk to Naomi Watts.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.834 --> 00:00:27.367
"Yeah, of course.
I love chip butties."

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:29.100
Yeah.
What is a chip butty?

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.200
-Okay, so --
-Or "chip butty."

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.100
-Butty, yeah, double T...
-Okay.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.934
-I-E or Y.
Um, so it basically

00:00:36.934 --> 00:00:40.267
is a delicious snack
that you devour

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:42.100
when you're super hungry.
-Yeah.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.968
-And, you know, it's often
after swimming lessons,

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:46.400
we used to have it as kids.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:50.734
And my grandfather decided
that this was a funny prank,

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:53.367
rather than giving us birthday
presents or Christmas presents,

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:56.734
he would make us delicious
chip butties

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:58.234
and put them on
the Christmas tree

00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:02.501
or wrap them up in tinfoil and
have them for birthday presents.

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:05.934
Anyway, it's french fries,

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.868
which we call chips
in England...

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:09.901
-Yeah.
Birthday presents, you said?

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:10.934
-Yes, yes.

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:12.000
-So you would get this
as a gift?

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.434
-Yes, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:14.501
-Did they, like,
wrap up the sandwich?

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.267
-We were happy about it!
-No, of course!

00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:17.701
It's great!
You open it up, "Oh, my --

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.100
it's a sandwich."
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.901
-Wow.
-It's a delicious sandwich.

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:22.968
-Oh, it's fantastic to get.
-It wasn't something

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:25.367
that he would be bothered
to make us, so...

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.300
Oh, you have it right here.
See?

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.501
This is --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:31.901
-Can I just -- okay.
It looks like --

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:37.033
Is it -- am I missing --
am I missing an ingredient?

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:40.501
-Well, is there salt and pepper
and vinegar on there?

00:01:40.501 --> 00:01:42.601
'Cause it's gonna
be dry otherwise.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.534
-Well, no, I think that'll
probably be on there, maybe.

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:46.300
-And butter.
Don't forget butter.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.100
-And "butta."
-Yeah, not butter.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.167
-Not butter.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:51.334
And it's butty, not a buddy.
-Exactly.

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:54.133
It's a chip butty -- "butty."
-The T's are T's, not are D's.

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:56.534
-Chip butty, with "buttah."
Not butter.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:57.667
-Exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:59.701
Are you gonna have a bite?
-Yeah, of course.

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:01.067
Would you like one,
or do you want me to --

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:02.367
I can just --
You look too nice.

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:04.200
-Yeah, I'm not gonna do that
with my red lipstick.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.934
-Yes, you look too good.
Yeah, here we go.

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:08.567
A chip butty, which is really,
honestly --

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:10.734
I feel like it's a sandwich
that's missing something.

00:02:10.734 --> 00:02:12.667
-Let me just --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.968
-It's --
I understand the idea of it.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.133
I just feel like --
-Do you ever put fries

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:18.667
in your sandwich?
-On a hamburger, yeah.

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:20.267
I feel like -- like,
at McDonald's, yeah.

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:22.033
But I feel like
that's the part I'm missing.

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:23.567
-Right, right.
-All right, let me just --

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:25.234
Here we go.
Do I put ketchup on it?

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:26.634
-Well --
-No, it has vinegar and salt.

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:27.701
-It has the vinegar and salt.

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:29.400
-It sounds like torture,
actually.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.667
It's very interesting.
No, here we go.

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:34.067
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:36.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:38.834
-Do you need to dip it?

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:42.133
-You need to do something to it.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.767
-Something -- maybe some beer.

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.167
-You know,
maybe if it was wrapped --

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:46.567
maybe if it was wrapped
in gift wrapping,

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:48.033
I'd be like, "Wow!
Unbelievable."

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:49.067
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:50.501
-This is my first butty.
-Here you go.

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:52.801
-Thank you.
-Good -- Good job for trying.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:54.834
-Of course I would try it.
-You need a beer chaser.

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:56.601
-I do need a beer chaser
with that.

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:59.167
I always love new foods, so
thank you for bringing that on.

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:02.567
But I -- that's the first time
and the last time, you know?

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:03.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:04.968
But -- joking.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:06.367
-My grandfather would be
turning in his grave.

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.234
-No! If grandpa made it for me,
are you kidding me?

00:03:08.234 --> 00:03:09.534
I would love it.
Are you kidding me?

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:11.400
But no.
All right, let's discuss.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.634
Next time, I'll --
-We can move on.

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:14.767
-Next time, I'll give you
a sandwich that I like.

00:03:14.767 --> 00:03:16.334
-Oh, God.
-I don't know

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:18.934
what that would be.
-Yeah, what would it be?

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.667
-Probably would be a hamburger
with french fries on it.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:23.968
With Halloween coming up,

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:26.501
do you get into
Halloween costumes?

00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:30.834
-Yeah. I never used to
do much for Halloween.

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:33.334
It's really an American thing.

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:35.801
-Oh, it's great.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:37.067
It's so fun.
-It's fun.

00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:38.834
-You're gonna love it, yeah.
You go door to door,

00:03:38.834 --> 00:03:40.701
and you wrap up sandwiches
and give it to each other.

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:42.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.501
-That could be the trick.
-"God, another butty, yeah."

00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:44.901
-That's the trick.
-You go, "Oh, my God.

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:48.467
I have 300 butties
in my pillow case."

00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:50.934
-"Don't knock on my door again."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.934 --> 00:03:52.400
-That'll be the last --
they'll throw eggs.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.901
Absolutely.
Don't give out butties.

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:56.868
But -- But I was like,
"Can you -- Can you send us

00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:59.501
a picture of a costume
if you ever got dressed up?"

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:01.167
-Yeah.
-And you did have a costume.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:04.667
Was this last year maybe?
-That was last year, yeah.

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:06.367
-That's very cute.
You were a cow.

00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:07.701
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:10.400
-Very -- come on.
That's the way to do it.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:13.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.067
Come on.
I thought you were gonna

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:16.634
go with something scarier.

00:04:16.634 --> 00:04:18.601
-Yeah, I've done scary before.
-You have?

00:04:18.601 --> 00:04:20.434
-Definitely.
I like to change it up.

00:04:20.434 --> 00:04:23.067
I just try to find whatever's
lying around in the house.

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:25.834
I didn't have that cow suit
lying around in the house.

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.834
-You -- You specially ordered
that cow suit.

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:30.567
-I did -- I did order that one.
-Yeah.

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:33.167
-But you do things --
we've talked about this --

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:34.667
where you're kind of
a daredevil, and I go,

00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:36.100
"Oh, I could never do that."

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.501
There was that one photo shoot
you did for "King Kong"...

00:04:38.501 --> 00:04:40.100
-Yeah.
-...on the Chrysler building.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.434
-That's right.
-Do you remember that?

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:43.000
-Oh, yeah.
I'll never forget that.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.501
-You stood on the top
of the Chrysler building.

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:46.701
-Yeah, right on the gargoyle.

00:04:46.701 --> 00:04:48.100
You know, the...
-Yeah.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.734
-...the bit that sticks out,
that's only about that wide.

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:52.934
-But that -- was it frightening?
Out of your mind?

00:04:52.934 --> 00:04:56.100
-Terrifying. I -- I don't know
what possessed me.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.667
But my agent and manager were
there, and they were saying,

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:01.567
"You don't have to do this,
you know? You don't."

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.367
And I was like, "Yeah,
why don't they Photoshop it?

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:05.467
This is insane."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:06.601
-Yeah, exactly, yeah, exactly.

00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:07.734
"You just greenscreen me
on top."

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:08.934
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:10.400
-I mean, the ape isn't real
in "King Kong."

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.701
Hello!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.701 --> 00:05:13.934
"Use the same technology.
Put me on top of anything."

00:05:13.934 --> 00:05:15.701
-Yeah, right -- well...
-None of these --

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:17.868
-It's one of those buildings.
-Yeah, you grab one.

00:05:17.868 --> 00:05:20.167
Yeah, yeah, exactly.
You could be on the top of it.

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:22.968
-And, um, and they said,
"No, they really want to do it.

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:24.534
It's a special story.

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:27.467
They want to know that it's
really happened."

00:05:27.467 --> 00:05:29.534
And I got up there,
and I looked down, I was like,

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:31.334
"No way.
I cannot do that."

00:05:31.334 --> 00:05:32.367
That's just -- makes me sick.

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:33.801
-You looked down.
That's the problem.

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:35.300
-Yeah.
-You can't look down.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:39.400
-And then I -- something came
over me, because my assistant,

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.934
who's kind of, at the time,

00:05:40.934 --> 00:05:44.734
was super athletic
and daredevil herself.

00:05:44.734 --> 00:05:46.234
And she said, "Oh, I'd do it."

00:05:46.234 --> 00:05:49.534
And I went, [ Gasps ]
"Okay, I have to do it.

00:05:49.534 --> 00:05:51.033
I can't be a chicken."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:52.167
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:53.467
-Are you competitive?

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:54.934
-I have a competitive streak,
yeah.

00:05:54.934 --> 00:05:56.267
-Yeah, you do, yeah.

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:58.200
You've never been that
competitive with me, have we?

00:05:58.200 --> 00:05:59.400
-Oh, well --
-A few times.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.767
-No, we played ping-pong.
What -- What's that game?

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:04.067
Beer pong.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.067 --> 00:06:06.167
-I was like, "I've never
called it ping-pong."

00:06:06.167 --> 00:06:07.534
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.534 --> 00:06:09.801
"We played ping, pong."
-I knew it wasn't ping.

00:06:09.801 --> 00:06:11.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.300
-But that's right,
we played beer bong.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.434
Oh, yeah, it was a little
competitive there.

00:06:13.434 --> 00:06:15.567
-I think I beat you.
-Yeah, I don't remember.

00:06:15.567 --> 00:06:19.601
But --
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.601 --> 00:06:21.767
I want to talk about
"The Watcher" because, man,

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:24.367
I think you -- you can do it,
you can do it all.

00:06:24.367 --> 00:06:26.767
But when it comes to the
thrilling, and the scariness,

00:06:26.767 --> 00:06:29.100
you nail it.
This thing is crazy.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:30.868
And it's super secretive,
by the way.

00:06:30.868 --> 00:06:33.501
-Yeah.
I'm not allowed to say anything.

00:06:33.501 --> 00:06:35.434
-I know. You're not.
But I'm allowed to.

00:06:35.434 --> 00:06:37.067
-Go on.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.067 --> 00:06:42.534
-I think it's about a family
who moves into a new house?

00:06:42.534 --> 00:06:45.434
-Yes.
-And they start getting notes...

00:06:45.434 --> 00:06:47.734
-Yes. From someone
in the neighborhood.

00:06:47.734 --> 00:06:49.267
And it's a story...
-Called The Watcher and says,

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:50.868
"I'm watching you."
-...a lot of New Yorkers

00:06:50.868 --> 00:06:53.901
are familiar with, or a lot of
Americans I suppose, yeah.

00:06:53.901 --> 00:06:55.467
-It's frightening.
-Yeah.

00:06:55.467 --> 00:06:57.200
-You get -- and it's like,
"I'm watching you.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:58.801
Signed, The Watcher"?
-Yeah.

00:06:58.801 --> 00:07:01.567
And they -- they've moved
to this home thinking it's gonna

00:07:01.567 --> 00:07:03.968
be their dream home, you know,
out in the suburbs

00:07:03.968 --> 00:07:07.200
with leafy green streets,
and, you know,

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.767
it's a beautiful house.

00:07:08.767 --> 00:07:11.701
-But it's so frightening.
-It goes terribly wrong.

00:07:11.701 --> 00:07:13.467
-It goes terribly wrong.
You couldn't say anything

00:07:13.467 --> 00:07:17.400
about the show, but last time
you were on our show --

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:20.567
Thank you, again --
you said you were doing

00:07:20.567 --> 00:07:22.534
pottery lessons for something
you were working on.

00:07:22.534 --> 00:07:23.767
-Oh, yeah.
-Can we say that you

00:07:23.767 --> 00:07:26.634
do pottery in this?
-Yes. You -- you're right.

00:07:26.634 --> 00:07:28.434
I debuted the reveal.
-I got the scoop?

00:07:28.434 --> 00:07:29.701
-Yes.
-I got the exclusive.

00:07:29.701 --> 00:07:32.033
Get ready for pottery, guys.
All over --

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:33.167
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.167 --> 00:07:34.901
No, but I was laughing,

00:07:34.901 --> 00:07:37.000
'cause we did it last time --
I was --

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.367
-You were great.

00:07:39.367 --> 00:07:41.367
-No, come on, now.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.367 --> 00:07:42.534
We actually, weirdly enough,

00:07:42.534 --> 00:07:44.734
we saved the pottery
of what we both made.

00:07:44.734 --> 00:07:46.834
We both -- We had a wheel
out there, we were learning.

00:07:46.834 --> 00:07:48.400
And I just wanted to show you
the finished products.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:49.501
You haven't seen it
since you've been here.

00:07:49.501 --> 00:07:53.334
-I haven't seen this.
-This is yours.

00:07:53.334 --> 00:07:56.334
-Well, very unfinished, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:56.334 --> 00:07:57.767
-Kind of cool that way.

00:07:57.767 --> 00:08:00.534
Actually, I love that.

00:08:00.534 --> 00:08:03.033
And then this is --
this one was mine.

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:06.167
[ Laughter ]
And I just thought...

00:08:06.167 --> 00:08:09.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
Very interesting.

00:08:09.534 --> 00:08:12.133
So they both turned out
kind of --

00:08:12.133 --> 00:08:14.167
-Not bad.
-Not bad at all.

00:08:14.167 --> 00:08:16.701
-Some improvements
could be made.

00:08:16.701 --> 00:08:18.834
-I want to give this to you.
-That's -- really?

00:08:18.834 --> 00:08:20.067
-For your birthday.
-This is beautiful.

00:08:20.067 --> 00:08:23.133
-Yeah. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:23.133 --> 00:08:24.834
-I could -- [ Laughs ]

00:08:24.834 --> 00:08:27.067
-I'm getting choked up.
-I love -- yeah.

00:08:27.067 --> 00:08:28.801
I love it.
-You -- what -- what is it?

00:08:28.801 --> 00:08:30.400
-I think --
-What could you do with it?

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:31.667
-What could we do with it?

00:08:31.667 --> 00:08:33.801
-You could, um,
hold your keys maybe in it.

00:08:33.801 --> 00:08:35.501
-Yeah, my jewelry.
I could put my rings.

00:08:35.501 --> 00:08:37.634
-Ooh, and incense!
Do you burn incense?

00:08:37.634 --> 00:08:39.601
-Yeah, I do.
-You do?

00:08:39.601 --> 00:08:41.000
-Yeah.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.033
That's perfect.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:42.033 --> 00:08:43.133
-Or a candle.

00:08:43.133 --> 00:08:44.934
-A candle -- yes.

00:08:44.934 --> 00:08:46.634
Put a candle in there.

00:08:46.634 --> 00:08:48.434
See, that's actually very artsy.

00:08:48.434 --> 00:08:49.701
[ Laughter ]

00:08:49.701 --> 00:08:51.868
It's almost like a fish mouth
or something.

00:08:51.868 --> 00:08:53.667
It looks like --
-It's some kind of vessel.

00:08:53.667 --> 00:08:55.868
-It looks like
the mouth of a bass.

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:56.968
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.968 --> 00:08:58.567
Like the --
-Looks like "The Scream."

00:08:58.567 --> 00:09:00.400
-Like -- like I'm an angler.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:02.734
You know, like --
Oh, I should do a photo shoot,

00:09:02.734 --> 00:09:05.968
like, fishing and be like, the
fish is coming out of the water.

00:09:05.968 --> 00:09:07.467
I mean, I got the beard.

00:09:07.467 --> 00:09:09.334
Now I just need
to start catching fish.

00:09:09.334 --> 00:09:11.133
This is actually unbelievable.

00:09:11.133 --> 00:09:12.334
This is where you put, like,
I don't know,

00:09:12.334 --> 00:09:13.901
extra hooks or bait
or something.

00:09:13.901 --> 00:09:15.133
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:09:15.133 --> 00:09:16.300
Well, anyways, this is for you.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:17.501
You could do whatever you like
to do with this.

00:09:17.501 --> 00:09:18.834
-I really love it, Jimmy.
-And we always love it

00:09:18.834 --> 00:09:20.267
when you come here.
Thank you so much.

00:09:20.267 --> 00:09:22.000
"The Watcher," everyone...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:25.000
...premieres October 13th
on Netflix.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.300
Stick around.
We'll be right back

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:27.801
with more "Tonight Show,"
everybody.

